-- #822, CROSS-MODULE half of the head-collision pin (adversarial review of PR
-- #1011).  Two graded interfaces in SEPARATE modules spelling their row-indexed head
-- the same way, with the Row in different slots.
--
-- Under the first cut of #822 the bare-name key made these fight: whichever module
-- was compiled first kept the entry and the other was rejected with
-- T-EFFECT-ARG-UNCOVERED — so the verdict flipped when the two import lines below
-- were swapped.  Both must now declare cleanly, in either order, because each
-- interface's kinds travel with it instead of living in a shared table.
--
-- (The same-file case is pinned by typecheck_error_fixtures/graded_head_name_collision.mdk;
-- this is the multi-module path that file's earlier claim was FALSE on.)
import ga.{GA, ga}
import gb.{GB, gb}

export both : Int
both = 1
